
  <sn><md>### Variable Assignment in C

**Variable assignment** means giving a value to a variable **after the variable has been declared**.

## Basic Syntax

```c
variable_name = value;
```

**Example**

```c
int age;    // Variable declaration

age = 20;   // Variable assignment
```

Here:

```text
age = 20;
 │    │
 │    └── Value being assigned
 └─────── Variable receiving the value
```

The `=` symbol is called the **assignment operator**.

It means:

&gt; Take the value on the right and store it in the variable on the left.
